{title: Dry Creek Bed}
{artist: Ozark Lanterns}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Dry creek bed where [D]the water used to sing
[E]Rusty bucket hanging f[A]rom a broken string
[A]Daddy said the rain [D]would always come
[E]Now we pray to every [A]passing drum
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D]Rain, rain, co[A]me on down
[E]Fill this dusty li[A]ttle town
[D]Rain, rain, co[A]me on down
[E]Wash the dry right out [A]of this ground
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]Clouds roll in and t[D]hen they roll away
[E]Preacher says that fai[A]th is all we pay
[A]Mama hangs the laundr[D]y anyway
[E]Hoping that she'll hav[A]e to bring it in today
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D]Rain, rain, co[A]me on down
[E]Fill this dusty li[A]ttle town
[D]Rain, rain, co[A]me on down
[E]Wash the dry right out [A]of this ground
{end_of_chorus}
